":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-06-22T12:33:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-25T18:38:10Z","closed_at":"2026-07-17T17:33:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120548","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120548","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120548.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120548.patch","merged_at":"2026-07-17T17:33:08Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #120542\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThis happened because a new `tile_proxy_object` was instantiated, which immediately destroyed the old one. However, the tile_inspector still held a pointer to that old object. When the new object was being processed, it was attempted to clean up and separate signals from the object that was already inactive, which caused a crash.\r\n\r\nI added `tile_inspector->edit(nullptr);` right before the proxy object gets overwritten. This forces the inspector to let go of the old object and clean up before the object actually gets wiped from memory.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organi